From: iPool bring-up <dev@ipool>
Date: Sun, 27 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] meson: build the DRI-loader stubs for wayland-only GBM/EGL

The gallium/targets/dril subdir builds the /usr/lib/dri/<driver>_dri.so
loader stubs (rockchip_dri.so, panfrost_dri.so, swrast_dri.so, ...) that
GBM/EGL dlopen at runtime. Upstream only builds it when GLX==dri or an
X11/XCB platform is enabled:

    if with_gallium and with_gbm
      if with_glx == 'dri' or with_platform_x11 or with_platform_xcb
        subdir('gallium/targets/dril')

On a wayland-only image (no x11 platform, glx forced disabled) none of
those hold, so the target is never built: /usr/lib/dri ends up empty and
GBM/EGL have no <driver>_dri.so to load, making eglInitialize() fail with
EGL_NOT_INITIALIZED. The stubs have no X11 dependency (they only link
libgallium + gbm), so build them for any gallium+gbm configuration.

Downstream (meta-ipool) fix for an RK3568 wayland/Weston boot2qt image.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/meson.build | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -152,9 +152,10 @@
   subdir('egl')
 endif
 if with_gallium and with_gbm
-  if with_glx == 'dri' or with_platform_x11 or with_platform_xcb
-    subdir('gallium/targets/dril')
-  endif
+  # meta-ipool: also build the DRI-loader stubs for wayland-only GBM/EGL.
+  # Upstream gates them behind glx=dri or x11/xcb; without them /usr/lib/dri
+  # is empty and eglInitialize() fails on a wayland-only image.
+  subdir('gallium/targets/dril')
 endif

 if with_gbm and with_dri2
